WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.368
(smacks)
- Ow.

00:00:01.368 --> 00:00:02.201
(laughing)

00:00:02.201 --> 00:00:03.520
That's enough BDSM in the kitchen.

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:04.932
Let's make some Matzo balls.

00:00:04.932 --> 00:00:06.024
(upbeat music)

00:00:06.024 --> 00:00:08.274
(creaking)

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:11.360
Hey everyone I'm Aaron.
- And I'm Leslie.

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:13.500
- We've been friends for a long time.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:14.333
But despite that,

00:00:14.333 --> 00:00:16.240
we haven't really cooked
for each other a lot,

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:18.600
which is weird because we
both care about food a lot.

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:19.470
- Oh yeah.

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:21.880
I grew up eating a lot
of Cantonese cooking

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:23.590
because my parents are
from southern China.

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:27.106
- And I am Jewish, so I grew
up eating a lot of Jewish food.

00:00:27.106 --> 00:00:29.300
So I thought it might
be cool if we went out,

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:32.000
got some groceries, cooked
some cute meals for each other,

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:33.830
and maybe in the process
learn a little bit

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:34.930
about each other's cultures.

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:36.290
- I think that sounds like a plan.

00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:38.453
- Are you ready?
- I'm so ready.

00:00:38.453 --> 00:00:41.120
(Chinese music)

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:45.020
You ready to get some Chinese groceries?

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:46.020
- Yeah, let's do it.

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:50.940
- We are in the Chinese supermarket.

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:52.544
We're about to get all the ingredients

00:00:52.544 --> 00:00:54.584
for my ketchup shrimp.

00:00:54.584 --> 00:00:59.229
(whooshing)
(popping)

00:00:59.229 --> 00:01:00.233
(beeping)

00:01:00.233 --> 00:01:01.189
- Awesome, thank you.

00:01:01.189 --> 00:01:02.450
So we got the ingredients
for the Chinese dishes

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:03.700
that Leslie's gonna be making

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:05.130
and now we just gotta get the food

00:01:05.130 --> 00:01:07.188
for the Jewish dishes that I'm gonna make.

00:01:07.188 --> 00:01:08.021
(record scratches)

00:01:08.021 --> 00:01:08.920
Okay but wait, hold up.

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:10.800
What do I mean when I say, "Jewish food."

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:13.030
Traditionally, observant Jews keep kosher,

00:01:13.030 --> 00:01:14.860
which means they can
only eat certain things.

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:17.330
The meals I'm making
today are Jewish dishes,

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:19.120
but I'm not using kosher ingredients.

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:21.080
They're not being cooked
in a kosher kitchen,

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:22.620
so they're not kosher.

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:25.346
They are however, delicious.

00:01:25.346 --> 00:01:28.596
(upbeat Chinese music)

00:01:32.710 --> 00:01:33.543
So I'm making something

00:01:33.543 --> 00:01:35.310
that's gonna be like very
classic, very standard.

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:37.570
Potato latkes, which normally
you eat during Hanukkah,

00:01:37.570 --> 00:01:39.150
but you can also eat them at any time.

00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:41.110
And another thing I'm gonna
make is Matzo ball soup,

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:43.930
which was something that
I ate every Friday night,

00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:44.992
every Shabbat.

00:01:44.992 --> 00:01:47.670
- I'm going to be making
ketchup fried shrimp.

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:50.240
So my dad made this for me
all the time growing up,

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:52.482
but I haven't had it in a while actually.

00:01:52.482 --> 00:01:54.050
- I'm a little nervous
'cause I've never actually

00:01:54.050 --> 00:01:55.253
made Matzo ball soup.

00:01:55.253 --> 00:01:58.027
- I haven't made ketchup fried shrimp.

00:01:58.027 --> 00:02:00.130
(record scratches)
(crickets chirping)

00:02:00.130 --> 00:02:01.840
- Are you ready?
- I'm ready.

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:03.160
(happy piano music)

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:06.350
What is your favorite memory
involving Matzo ball soup?

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:08.760
- Growing up, my family
wasn't super religious,

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:12.170
but we did pretty consistently
recognize Shabbat,

00:02:12.170 --> 00:02:15.310
a time of the week where
you slow down and you rest.

00:02:15.310 --> 00:02:16.700
Pretty much every Shabbat dinner

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:17.780
had to have Matzo ball soup.

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:19.350
It was like a staple, it was like a given.

00:02:19.350 --> 00:02:21.991
(happy piano music)

00:02:21.991 --> 00:02:22.824
(lid clatters)

00:02:22.824 --> 00:02:24.070
Latke dance, makin' latkes.

00:02:24.070 --> 00:02:27.270
- Why'd you pick latkes?
- Because latkes are something

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:29.280
you traditionally eat during Hanukkah.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:31.460
Growing up as a kid, some
of my favorite memories

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:32.320
are from Hanukkah.

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:34.530
Just being with your
family and getting presents

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:35.880
and eating good food.

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:38.210
And it's such a fun holiday.

00:02:38.210 --> 00:02:39.200
- Just do it to taste.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:41.790
That's how my parents, my grandma.

00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:43.945
- This is actually (beeps) delicious.

00:02:43.945 --> 00:02:44.778
Oh my (beeps) God.

00:02:44.778 --> 00:02:46.090
Just ketchup and some tomato paste

00:02:46.090 --> 00:02:48.180
and soy sauce.
- Right?

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:49.450
- But it's so good.

00:02:49.450 --> 00:02:51.798
- So you can just go ahead
and cut off the heads.

00:02:51.798 --> 00:02:53.961
(popping)
cut it.

00:02:53.961 --> 00:02:54.906
(gasps)
- Oh.

00:02:54.906 --> 00:02:55.860
- Oh my.

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:56.693
So dramatic.
- Oh no.

00:02:56.693 --> 00:02:58.854
Shrimpy, I'm so sorry.

00:02:58.854 --> 00:03:00.220
(sighs)

00:03:00.220 --> 00:03:02.240
- We're gonna put all of
the ginger into the pan.

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:05.660
My dad is from Guangzhou,
China, which is a port city.

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:07.700
It's really close to the ocean.

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:10.945
I just remember sitting down at dinner

00:03:10.945 --> 00:03:13.290
and then getting so
excited when I found out

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:15.480
that he made ketchup fried shrimp.

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:17.900
I feel so lucky to have
grown up with his cooking

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:19.610
'cause he got that training in China

00:03:19.610 --> 00:03:21.180
and now when he makes dinner for us,

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:23.260
he makes six or seven dishes.

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:24.560
It's ridiculous.

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:27.143
(upbeat music)

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:30.180
- Leslie, this looks amazing.

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:31.600
- I know, ready to eat it?

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:34.827
- Yeah.
(mysterious music)

00:03:34.827 --> 00:03:35.660
(slurping)

00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:36.640
- This is really good.

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:38.270
- The Matzo balls are a little dense.

00:03:38.270 --> 00:03:41.110
If it had been my mom, they'd
probably be a little fluffier.

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:41.943
Ta-da.

00:03:44.195 --> 00:03:45.073
- [Leslie And Arron] Mm-mm.

00:03:45.073 --> 00:03:47.620
- Okay this just tastes like Judaism.

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:49.220
- I thought this would taste so weird

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:51.433
with applesauce but it works.

00:03:51.433 --> 00:03:52.938
- The sweetness of the applesauce,

00:03:52.938 --> 00:03:55.522
and the tanginess of the sour cream,

00:03:55.522 --> 00:03:59.820
and the salty, oily, potato-y,
carby-ness of the latke.

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:01.504
It just makes sense.

00:04:01.504 --> 00:04:03.890
(gasps)
- Ta-da.

00:04:03.890 --> 00:04:04.850
Let's dig in.

00:04:04.850 --> 00:04:05.767
- This is actually really good.

00:04:05.767 --> 00:04:08.412
- I'm so happy I got to
introduce you to this new dish.

00:04:08.412 --> 00:04:10.434
- I think I'm eating a piece
of shell from the shrimp,

00:04:10.434 --> 00:04:11.267
but I don't even care
'cause it's still good.

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:14.560
- I kinda just wanna finish this TBH.

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:18.610
It was just really nice
getting to try foods

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:19.780
that you grew up with.

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:21.020
- China's such a huge country

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:23.010
and there's so many different
regions and ethnic groups

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:23.843
and it was nice to learn

00:04:23.843 --> 00:04:26.080
about where specifically
your family came from

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:29.180
and the kinds of things
that you grew up with.

00:04:29.180 --> 00:04:30.682
- Aaron?
- Yeah?

00:04:30.682 --> 00:04:32.635
- I'm so happy you're my friend.

00:04:32.635 --> 00:04:34.700
(sighs)

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:36.311
- Leslie, I'm happy you're my friend.

00:04:36.311 --> 00:04:38.224
(sighs)
I think we make a good team.

00:04:38.224 --> 00:04:41.767
- I agree.
(groans)

00:04:41.767 --> 00:04:44.267
(happy music)

00:04:53.702 --> 00:04:55.705
(whooshing)
(creaking)

